rem Tangents to an ellipse
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=246
rem Count the lattice points P from
rem which the two tangents to the
rem ellipse of points equidistant from
rem the circle of radius Radius about M
rem and from G meet at more than 45
rem degrees; G is Gap to the right of M,
rem Gap even

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Radius integer = 15000
option Gap integer = 10000

rem The ellipse has foci M and G and
rem major axis Radius, so with the
rem centre as origin A = (Radius / 2)^2
rem and B = A - (Gap / 2)^2 are its
rem squares of the semi-axes. The
rem tangents from (x, y) meet at an
rem angle above 45 degrees when it lies
rem outside the ellipse, B x^2 + A y^2 >
rem A B, and y^2 + x^2 - 3 A - B < 2
rem sqrt(R), where R = 2 A^2 - (A - B)
rem x^2 is positive only for a limited
rem x. The y between those bounds,
rem either sign, are counted for each x
rem with exact integer roots.
A = (Radius // 2) ** 2
B = A - (Gap // 2) ** 2
Lim = ((2 * A * A) // (A - B)) isqrt + 1
X = 0 - Lim to Lim array
R = 2 * A * A - (A - B) * X * X
K = 3 * A + B - X * X
Pos = (4 * R - 1) 0 max
W = Pos isqrt
Real = R greater 0
Ok = Real and (K + W at least 0)
Base = (K + W) 0 max
Top = Base isqrt
N = B * (A - X * X)
Fl = (N // A) 0 max
Under = Fl isqrt + 1
Low = (N less 0) choose 0 Under
Cnt = Top - Low + 1
Zero = Low equal 0
Per = 2 * Cnt - (Zero choose 1 0)
Used = Ok and (Top at least Low)
Answer = (Used choose Per 0) sum
Answer print
